; Included by review.journal: an earlier file whose last transactions fall
; inside the review window, so a batch can span two files and a read-only
; include can be counted as "not editable".
;
; An `=` rule whose output is uncategorised. Only `--auto` applies it (the
; core tests that read the journal as written never see it fire): then the
; reviewed `Blue Bottle Coffee` rename (2026-09-01, in review.journal) gains
; generated `(expenses:unknown)` postings and is unknown again (plan 32
; amendment A). It lives here rather than in review.journal so the main file
; keeps no `=` rule of its own: an included file's rules apply journal-wide.

= desc:coffee$
    (expenses:unknown)  *1

